build:

 make            (or: src/mk.sh [i386 | amd64 | 32 | 64] [clean | debug])

install (Linux):

 sudo make install [BINDIR=dir] [DESTDIR=dir]

 'make install' grants cap_net_admin to the binary via setcap when
 available, so tap mode (-e) works for unprivileged users. Without it,
 tap mode requires root; udp mode (default) needs no privileges.
 The -n option disables vpcs configuring the host tap interface.

